Places a stellux swapchain's buffers by the read flag of the GPU_INFO it is
created under: in host-visible system memory while stlxdm reads them with
the CPU, and in video memory the CPU cannot map while stlxdm reads them with
the GPU, which reads video memory fastest, or in system memory on a device
without such a type. A GPU_INFO that changes the read flags makes the
swapchain out of date: its acquires and presents, and present waits for a
present it refused, return VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR, so the program
recreates it in the placement now asked.

